{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence","id":1353993,"title":"How long does it normally take various Exalted to reach new levels of Essence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-09T16:33:09-08:00","id":1353993,"title":"How long does it normally take various Exalted to reach new levels of Essence?","content":"I am curious as to how fast the various Exalts tend to grow in power (Essence) when they are not PCs. I thought I saw a chart of how quickly different Exalts are likely to develop the different levels of Essence, but I can't seem to find it anywhere now.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I am looking for this information is because I am trying to gauge how powerful a Lunar would be 50 years after Exaltation, assuming the Lunar is reasonably active in the world (building a power base and such).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:38:46-08:00","id":1353994,"title":"","content":"I know 2e had particular ideas about how fast PC's could advance. But I don't know if 3e was so specific.<br /> <br /> If I was to make an uneducated guess, I'd say that the *average* 50-year-old Lunar (inasmuch as such things exist) is probably Essence 3. A true up-and-coming legend might be sitting comfortably at 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T17:37:03-08:00","id":1354013,"title":"","content":"I think it depends a lot on particular exalts. Cynis Cogen is nearing the end of his life as a party animal and he's Essence 3, Ledaal Kes is young and also 3, Then you've got Sesus Nezzegar, who's not that old and he's Essence 4, and Cynis Borok, who's a major screwup and only 2. So it seems like maybe increasing essence is tied to ambition?<br /> <br /> Looking at Lunars all the first age surviving elders are 6-7, with some younger elders being 4. So it looks like Essence 2 comes really easily, maybe after a year of exaltation or less. Then three is something that will come with time over maybe a century, but if they try for it a decade or two. Four only comes if you put work into it, and only after several decades. Then 5 is only for the try-hards who are almost two centuries at least, and past that you're generally looking at people who've seen the turning off an age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T19:39:39-08:00","id":1354040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence#post1353993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious as to how fast the various Exalts tend to grow in power (Essence) when they are not PCs. I thought I saw a chart of how quickly different Exalts are likely to develop the different levels of Essence, but I can't seem to find it anywhere now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a sidebar towards the end of the core book's Traits chapter, around the part talking about the mechanical and gameplay side of developing Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T19:40:55-08:00","id":1354041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354013#post1354013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it depends a lot on particular exalts. Cynis Cogen is nearing the end of his life as a party animal and he's Essence 3, Ledaal Kes is young and also 3, Then you've got Sesus Nezzegar, who's not that old and he's Essence 4, and Cynis Borok, who's a major screwup and only 2. So it seems like maybe increasing essence is tied to ambition?<br /> <br /> Looking at Lunars all the first age surviving elders are 6-7, with some younger elders being 4. So it looks like Essence 2 comes really easily, maybe after a year of exaltation or less. Then three is something that will come with time over maybe a century, but if they try for it a decade or two. Four only comes if you put work into it, and only after several decades. Then 5 is only for the try-hards who are almost two centuries at least, and past that you're generally looking at people who've seen the turning off an age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance has said there might be First Age Lunars still at Essence 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T19:56:28-08:00","id":1354044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354041#post1354041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vance has said there might be First Age Lunars still at Essence 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but they\u2019re probably not Raksi levels of \u201cGive me more power! MOAR I SAY!\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T20:10:07-08:00","id":1354048,"title":"","content":"My own estimate is that certain Essence levels represent natural plateaus for many Exalts, which they can stay at for decades or even centuries. I think Essence 3 and 5 are both plateaus of this sort, with 4 being somewhat less of one, but still something possible to stay at for quite a long time. The upshot of this is that there probably isn't a really meaningful &quot;average time&quot; that an Exalt spends at a given level. Some could only take a few years to break through Essence 3, while others could hover there for centuries.<br /> <br /> I <i>do </i>think that Dragonbloods probably get to Essence 3 and higher Essence levels a bit faster than other Exalts do, statistically speaking. I think their shorter lifespans probably contribute a bit of sense of urgency to cultivating their power, and their larger population and more developed support network mean that it's more plausible for them to retreat from the world in an appropriate location for the weeks or months required. <br /> <br /> So, to provide my own answer, I'd guess that about 50% of Lunars, Solars, Abyssals, and other &quot;Celestial&quot; Exalted who reach 100 years old are probably Essence 3, whereas more like 75% or more of Dragonbloods are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T02:25:30-08:00","id":1354093,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I don't really agree, because I don't think that when a heroic warrior exalts as a Solar defending her tribe from the forces of the Black Pharoah Garbed In Hate, knowing basically nothing about Solars except some garbled legends, she's going to go &quot;oh, I've got thousands of years to live, no big urgency&quot;. I very much doubt most Solars know they've got an extended lifespan. And Sidereals hardly have time to chill, as Heaven's top secret agents who are also secretly controlling the world from the shadows on their vacation time.<br /> <br /> You are right about Dynastic society being more set up to help people cultivate their essence though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T02:27:47-08:00","id":1354094,"title":"","content":"Oh, and here is the part Isator was referring to:<br /> &quot;On average, most Celestial Exalts who don\u2019t fall to the Wyld Hunt in their early days manage to reach Essence 3,<br /> though it takes decades or longer for many to get there. Of those that survive beyond the span of a mortal lifetime,<br /> a significant number eventually reach Essence 4. Essence 5 is a mark of extreme prowess, vanishingly rare<br /> among the ranks of the comparatively short-lived Dragon-Blooded and noteworthy even among centuries-old<br /> elder Celestial Exalted. To achieve such power in a matter of years rather than decades or centuries is the mark<br /> of a great prodigy.<br /> To climb beyond the earth-shaking power of Essence 5 to even greater heights was a remarkable feat even for the<br /> ancient heroes of the First Age, and such matters are beyond the scope of this book.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T04:29:37-08:00","id":1354106,"title":"","content":"So I think taking everything into account, your 50 years exalted lunar would probably be essence 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T05:02:44-08:00","id":1354114,"title":"","content":"That seems reasonable. They might only be Essence 2 if they haven't been doing much (for a Lunar!), or maybe if they're a prodigy Essence 4. They're probably not Essence 1, and they're almost certainly not Essence 5.<br /> <br /> The one described (reasonably active) sounds like Essence 3 to me.<br /> <br /> I find this chart very useful for NPCs actually (much more than 2nd ed's). I make most NPCs who are older than the PCs Essence 3, Elders who've been around centuries Essence 4, and Essence 5 for NPCs who are a millenia or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T05:04:36-08:00","id":1354115,"title":"","content":"It's just suddenly occurred to me that, based on age, the Deathlords ought to be Essence 4-6, maybe 7 at most...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T06:06:08-08:00","id":1354127,"title":"","content":"Yeah but who knows what funky shit becoming a deathlord does to you.<br /> <br /> Also they probably work more off the ghost power scale than the exalt one. That makes 8s and 9s more manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T06:18:31-08:00","id":1354129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354115#post1354115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just suddenly occurred to me that, based on age, the Deathlords ought to be Essence 4-6, maybe 7 at most...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if one assumed that they all started at Essence 1.<br /> <br /> Still, I think Deathlords ought to work more like spirits with regards to the level of their Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T08:18:59-08:00","id":1354153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354048#post1354048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do </i>think that Dragonbloods probably get to Essence 3 and higher Essence levels a bit faster than other Exalts do, statistically speaking. I think their shorter lifespans probably contribute a bit of sense of urgency to cultivating their power, and their larger population and more developed support network mean that it's more plausible for them to retreat from the world in an appropriate location for the weeks or months required.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a significant change from the past. I cant quote exact sources, but in past editions DBs didnt advance very quickly, not just for XP reasons, but cultural reasons as well. The typical dragon-blooded is much more down to earth than the celestial exalts. They have mundane worries like ruling creation and managing the family, and generally being nobility. So they spend their time focused on mundane stuff rather than cultivating thier essence. As a result DBs rarely exceeded Essence 3. Almost all achieved Essence 3 in their lifetime, but that still takes the typical Dragon-Blooded a century. A notable exception would be Immaculate Monks who spend a lot of time meditating and cultivating their essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T08:28:30-08:00","id":1354158,"title":"","content":"I could see it being true for the more civilised portions of the First Age where &quot;you're going to live for thousands of years, what's the rush!&quot; might carry some weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T08:33:30-08:00","id":1354161,"title":"","content":"They have a decades head start of getting to essence 3 compared to most exalted at least, so that probably helps a bit. <br /> <br /> I never got the impression that they progress slower or faster if you count from the moment of exaltation though. It takes a couple of centuries to get to essence 4, so only the oldest dragon blooded and rare prodigies have it, and of those that would achieve essence 5 if they lived long enough most die of old age before they get the chance, leaving <i>only</i> the rare prodigies among them to manage it. <br /> <br /> And I think the books bear that out. Most of the 200-300 year old noteworthy dragon blooded we see are essence 4, Mnemon and I think Arada are 5, and they're really big names, and Ledaal Kes, himself a prodigy who will probably be essence 5 someday, is only essence 3 right now cos he's in his 60s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T09:13:49-08:00","id":1354176,"title":"","content":"If you look at the Dragon-Blooded npcs, Essence correlates strongly with age. Most DB npcs with high essence are actually older than the expected lifespan of a Dragon-Blooded. This implies that Dragon-Blooded can extend their life by cultivating Essence and such high essence is rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T10:11:10-08:00","id":1354191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354129#post1354129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if one assumed that they all started at Essence 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I said 5-7 was because I was counting their lives as Solars too, so yes.<br /> <br /> And with spirits, well, people like Ahlat were already strong in the Primordial War, and have had 5000 years since.<br /> <br /> Not to say that, if it works well, the Deathlords can't be Essence 9, just that if they were, say, Essence 6, that would be quite reasonable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T10:15:07-08:00","id":1354193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354158#post1354158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it being true for the more civilised portions of the First Age where &quot;you're going to live for thousands of years, what's the rush!&quot; might carry some weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would definitely make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a decades head start of getting to essence 3 compared to most exalted at least, so that probably helps a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got the impression that they progress slower or faster if you count from the moment of exaltation though.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, they mechanically need more experience than Celestials to get to higher Essence, which I assume represents an in-game increased difficulty of getting high essence.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T10:19:08-08:00","id":1354195,"title":"","content":"Nephwracks are Essence 5 and pretty badass. Mostly as sorcerers and commanders but an Essence 7 Deathlord could be pretty epic by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T11:05:29-08:00","id":1354210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354191#post1354191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with spirits, well, people like Ahlat were already strong in the Primordial War, and have had 5000 years since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahlat is Essence whatever because he's a Directional God of War. His age is irrelevant. His efforts (beyond those put into being appointed as Directional God of War) are irrelevant.<br /> <br /> On a similar token, there's more liberty to give spirits Essence above 5 because it carries far less weight than doing it with the Exalted owing to their more narrow power. It signifies their place in the overall spiritual hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Deathlords ought to be more like spirits than Exalted, meaning that while I don't expect many to be as high as 9, that would carry hardly much more puissance than Ryzala, Lady of Bureaucracy and Paperwork possesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T11:08:29-08:00","id":1354211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354176#post1354176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the Dragon-Blooded npcs, Essence correlates strongly with age. Most DB npcs with high essence are actually older than the expected lifespan of a Dragon-Blooded. This implies that Dragon-Blooded can extend their life by cultivating Essence and such high essence is rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the correlation goes the other way around; sorcery, anagathics and Artifacts that extend lifespan provide the opportunity in which to grow so powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T15:16:47-08:00","id":1354251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354211#post1354211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the correlation goes the other way around; sorcery, anagathics and Artifacts that extend lifespan provide the opportunity in which to grow so powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saibok Gauto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:51:20-08:00","id":1354469,"title":"","content":"Oh wow. It takes decades to reach essence 3?<br /> <br /> My story has a Medicine supernal that hits essence 3 after 6 months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T15:00:01-08:00","id":1354473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354469#post1354469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow. It takes decades to reach essence 3?<br /> <br /> My story has a Medicine supernal that hits essence 3 after 6 months.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally it takes decades to get to Essence 3 and centuries to get to 4-5, but for player characters those timeframes are often vastly reduced. In the most extreme case of DBs it takes about 65 sessions of Exalted to gain enough xp to get to Essence 5, but that could take place in the span of a year or two, maybe even less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T17:45:21-08:00","id":1354500,"title":"","content":"PC's are assumed to always be moving forward and striving for a goal, never slowing down or pausing (Or that time is skipped and no exp is granted as Down time.) As such, Players grow much much faster than npc's tend to. You don't grow working a 9-5 and being lazy in your leisure time. I doubt Exalted grow when they are on vacation and just sunbathing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T18:53:32-08:00","id":1354508,"title":"","content":"I think 2e lore mentioned that getting to E5 before your first century was almost unheard of. <br /> <br /> Also going with that, there's a Solar who is famous for being the first to die of old age and after that everyone suddenly had to get up off their ass and start moving, so who even knows if timelines matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T02:28:38-08:00","id":1354540,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but in 2e it was literally impossible to achieve certain essence levels before a certain age, which is a concept 3e dumped.<br /> <br /> And yeah, those incredible prodigies that get super powerful super quick? Every single PC is one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T09:49:29-08:00","id":1355202,"title":"","content":"Listening to all of this, I think I will add a little additional information.<br /> <br /> The campaign I hope to run will be a Dragon-Blooded focused one... specifically on the survivors of a successful but costly Wyld Hunt. The players at this time will be fresh from graduation at their respective Secondary Schools (or the equivalent there of) and will have joined this Wyld Hunt to gain some experience for their future careers (looks great on a resume, so to speak). They will be going after a small but growing cult that seems to have fallen under the sway of an Anathema (presumed to be a Solar). What they find however is that the Cult worships a Solar and Lunar pair... with the Lunar being a powerful Witch/Sorceress (Essence 5 No Moon Caste) while the Solar is a competent Warrior-Priest (Essence 2 Zenith Caste). While the Wyld Hunt easily decimates the mortal followers of the Anathema (with the Players taking the lead in this part), the power of the two Anathema is such that it more than compensates and decimates the strength of the Wyld Hunt. By the end of the first encounter, the Cult is shattered, the forces of the Wyld Hunt are diminished significantly, the two Anathema escape (but are drained and wounded) and the players are the only surviving Exalts from the Hunt (though there is secretly a wounded and drained Sidereal survivor too). The players will have to decide if the fails and the go to get reinforcements (allowing the Anathema time to recover) or press on to get the job done (this may be their best and only chance to finish the Anathema off). Hopefully, the players will charge in to finish the job... which will see the Solar captured and the Lunar killed. The Solar will be brought to the Scarlet Empress (or other authority that might be able to save the soul of the person possessed by the Anathema) for imprisonment.<br /> <br /> After this, there will be a 50 year time skip (which may be played out in short one-shot adventures over a few sessions, with each taking place years apart as events bring the Sworn Brotherhood back together... or test their bonds to each other). I am thinking of granting players a small EXP reward for this period to show how their characters have progressed in this period... depending on how much they have gained through their first Hunt and the small adventures between. Ideally, when we resume the main story, they should be close to reaching Essence 4 (if they already haven't).<br /> <br /> When the main story resumes, the players will be in the present setting, with the Empress having vanished about 3 years ago and the Realm inching ever closer to Civil War while more and more Threshold States rebel against the oppressive taxation of the Great Houses. Into this mess comes rumors of a barbaric Warlord raising an army to reunite the nation the players decimated 50 years ago... suggesting that the Lunar has reincarnated and reinvented themselves as a Full Moon Caste (Essence 4 due to constant activity) with a massive and growing army. The also learn that the Solar they imprisoned (and likely thought long dead) has managed to escape its imprisonment and was able to flee to the Threshold (and is likely looking to join up with the Lunar... once the learn of each other). Like the Lunar, the Solar has become more powerful than before, but due to its imprisonment, it isn't as powerful as the Lunar (Solar is only Essence 3). Knowing that their best chance for dealing with these threats is to move quickly and hunt them down before they can join up again, the only resources the players will likely be able to call upon is that the are personally responsible for (troops and such loyal to them) as any nation they are part of is likely gearing up to deal with the impending Realm civil war.<br /> <br /> In short, the Second Hunt will more or less reverse the roles of the players. Where they were well backed and supplied by the Wyld Hunt the first time, their resources in this one is more limited and finite. Where before they were going up against mostly untrained combatants, this time they are fighting a trained (though not an elite) army. The only thing really in their favor is that they are more experienced than before, but the Anathema have also learned to fight more effectively than they did before. The Lunar may not have access to the same level of Sorcery as before... which is where the Zenith comes in (it was able to recover enough confiscated occult material from where it was imprisoned to help it master Celestial Circle Sorcery... it learned Terrestrial Circle from the Lunar 50 years prior). This should make the rematch a lot more interesting and uncertain. While it is very possible for the players to triumph and put these threats down for a time (they will reincarnate again and again), it is also possible that this will be their final battle... their final stand against the chaos and darkness engulfing Creation. There is also the possibility that they come up with another option that I haven't thought of yet (such as maybe discovering an even greater threat that can only be defeated if they join forces with the Anathema... though what could cause this outcome?).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I just wanted to be sure that 50 years is enough time for a Lunar that is reasonably active (as a warlord) could attain Essence 4 in 50 years. I think that I might be pushing it to raise the Solar to Essence 3 in the same time frame, given its imprisonment (likely with devices to drain it of Essence to prevent escape). As for the players, I think having them close to (or having just reached Essence 4) puts them in a reasonable place for this final part of the campaign.<br /> <br /> The general rule I have been going with is that Dragon-Bloods reach Essence 2 by the time they finish Secondary School, Essence 3 by the time they finish their first tour of duty, Essence 4 around the time of their first century... and Essence 5 around their 2nd century. For Solars, they usually reach Essence 2 within a year of Exaltation, Essence 3 within a decade, Essence 4 within a mortal's lifespan and Essence 5 after a century or more (Essence 6 requires at least a few centuries to a millennium). Lunars are roughly the same, as would Abyssals and Infernals (though these two have access to resources that can speed this up). Sidereal likely retain teaching techniques that allow them to reach Essence two by the end of their training (a year or two) and can reach Essence 3 or 4 within the first century after Exaltation... Essence 5+ likely requires centuries to attain under normal conditions. Alchemicals likely follow a similar pattern. I don't know enough about the newer Exalts (Exigents, Liminals and even Getimians) to be sure of their tendencies and initial power levels to know their Essence growth with any reasonable reliability (Exigents alone are so varied in power levels and even lifespans to be hard to generalize in any fashion). These generalities of course assume a reasonable level of activity without world-shaking events that could accelerate this (or reset them if killed).<br /> <br /> Players of course defy these generalities as a mater of course, since they tend to be the main focus of their stories and thus accomplish more in a reasonable short period of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:15:29-08:00","id":1355247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353993-how-long-does-it-normally-take-various-exalted-to-reach-new-levels-of-essence?p=1354251#post1354251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saibok Gauto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saibok Gauto and Well-Tended Garden of the Soul are not really relevant to a discussion of Third Edition. I assumed you were talking about Essence 5 Mnemon and the conditions in which the Scarlet Empress has the means to reach whatever elder Essence she was packing at least as late as the Calibration between RY 761 and 2.<br /> <br /> Mind, Gauto was a case in which higher Essence opens the door, but his longevity owed a lot more to an ascetic lifestyle that kept the difficulty to stay alive from outstripping whatever dice pool was rolled to sustain him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}